  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tBookkeeping\n\t\tBookkeeping Help Guide\n\n### How to add transactions to the Bank manually?\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Thu, 19 Aug, 2021 at  4:29 PM\n\n\t\tLocation:  Bookkeeping module > Dashboard > Client specific > Bank > Dashboard\n\nClick here to watch how to manually post a bank statement \n\nHelp Guide: \n\nPlease click on your bank account\n\nThen click manual import in the top right hand corner\n\nplease fill out the transactions as needed\n\nYou can delete rows by using the bin button\n\nYou can add rows by clicking the + Row button\n\nThen click Save \n\nThese transactions will now sit on the dashboard. These are not reconciled\n\nPlease click here to find out how to reconcile transactions\n\nManually\nAutomatically\nMultiple transactions\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
